jitInlineBindT -- SEQ 396 B1 (Tony): the inline arm's run-time argument bind and its channel bracket (option (c)). Each
ibF* is its own compiled function (a self-call) that first calls an INLINED callee with its argument, then calls itself,
then reads its own `argument` field at run time in a handed-over cerr. The interpreted road un-binds every call, so each
section prints 0 1 2. Under the cure the inline arm binds at run time and pushes the pending entry; the pop at the
region's join un-binds it. Remove the pop and the stack goes out of step: a self-call's restore pops the INLINED callee's
entry instead of its own, and the caller reads the callee's argument. Sections: IB-1 the fall-through; IB-2 the callee
ends on a refused statement (an iterate over a count); IB-3 the callee ends on a handed-over mid-body return (ibL carries
code, so `return ibL` is a list read), IB-5 its tail never ran; IB-4 a nested inline (ibXn inlines ibX). Trunk at seal 194
(no inline bind yet): every section 0 1 2 = the twin. The refusal NAMES differ between the roads (argSlot / Token,
tempField); the counts are pinned, not the names.
